**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Operator scratch dir — local WIP notes, ad-hoc probes, recovery files.
# Persists across sessions intentionally; never committed.
.scratch/

# Workstation tunnel daemon hardcodes the real seedbox FQDN — treat as secret.
scripts/manitoba-tunnel.ps1

# Workstation-only audit script. NOT excluded for secrets — the old comment here
# claimed it "hardcodes the real seedbox FQDN", which was copied from the tunnel
# entry above and is false: Resolve-SshHost reads secrets/seedbox.ssh-host (or
# $env:QFLIX_SSH_HOST) at runtime and throws rather than guess. Verified clean
# 2026-07-29 — no FQDN, token, webhook or credential in the file.
# It stays out of git because it is operator-local tooling that runs on the
# workstation, not on the box, and the repo is public.
# Backup: scripts/local-llm/backup-untracked.ps1, hourly via the scheduled task
# \Archangel\Backups\QFlix-Untracked-Backup. It reads the file list from
# manifest/audit-scope.yaml surface S2 (so enrolling a member there enrols it in
# the backup), writes into the same B:\BAKS\Documents mirror the daily
# Backup-Documents /MIR run uses, ALSO keeps a content-addressed version history
# at B:\BAKS\qflix-untracked-history, and SHA256-verifies all three. It exits 1
# on divergence and 2 when it cannot tell, and pages Discord either way.
# Until 2026-08-03 the only backup was that daily /MIR — a mirror, not history,
# with nothing verifying it. Measured that day: the mirror was 22 hours and two
# edits behind this file and every surface reported success.
scripts/local-llm/qflix-rea.ps1

# Staging dir for the 2026-05-11 inventory-driven cleanup; safe to delete once
# the operator confirms nothing was accidentally swept.
.purged-*/
.admin-key/
